Chapter: RecordFieldSilence

 A field left OUT came back as zero, and zero is a plausible value for
 an integer, an empty list and a null pointer alike, so nothing
 downstream could tell it was never set. That cost a real
 memory-corruption bug -- net-io-send-chunk rebuilt a TcpTransportState
 naming four of its seven fields, so every send zeroed a raw heap
 address and the next inbound frame wrote bytes off the wire to
 physical address 0, over the IDT.

Section: Definitions

  Point = record {
   x : Integer,
   y : Integer
  }

  missing-one : Point
  missing-one = Point { x = 1 }

  wrong-name : Point
  wrong-name = Point { x = 1, z = 2 }

  opening : Integer = 0
